      "content": "Even though it's possible that this headache is a severe migraine, the suddenness and intensity of your pain raise concerns that may not be addressed by self-medicating. \"Really bad migraines\" can indeed become life-threatening if they are atypical presentations of more serious conditions. It's crucial to differentiate because many life-threatening conditions have very limited time windows in which they are treatable effectively. Professional assessment not only serves to rule out these conditions but also ensures that if it is a migraine, your elevated treatment plan is safe and appropriate. High doses of over-the-counter medication may offer some temporary relief, but without comprehensive medical evaluation, you're unable to be certain you're not facing a more severe issue. The cost of avoiding unnecessary ER visits is significantly less than ignoring potential warning signs that could require expensive and aggressive treatments in the future. Prioritizing your health and safety is essential. If you're still concerned about the cost, many hospitals offer financial assistance or payment plans, and in many urgent cases, they can also prioritize care based on the likelihood of severe conditions. The cost of missing a potentially critical diagnosis is generally much greater than the ER visit. Always trust your instincts if something feels wrong, and seek prompt medical attention.",
